				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/111/483/637/191/758/954/original/638607630fb38813.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-09T21:09:20.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I remember that a wml card could only hold a maximum of characters, including the markup. Due to this long texts had to be split into multiple cards. Iow, one had to count characters in a text and subtract markup one would use to know where to cut the text for a card. </p><p>And; if one got that wrong the markup could end up being cut by the mobile gateway on the way out to the user.</p><p>And if that did happen it all would crash on the client due to invalid xml.</p><p>Boy. Yeah. FML!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
